/**
 * Direct-style I/O with the `Console` effect.
 *
 * `readLine` yields an `Option[String]` and `printLine` consumes a plain `String`, yet both perform `Console`.
 * Writing the one out of the other directly works because an effect operation is an ordinary call: it runs where it
 * is written. Neither `echo` nor `main` names an implementation — the platform's synthesized entry point binds the
 * default `implement Console` for the `uses Console` of `main`, and a test would bind its own with `with`.
 *
 * The `Option` is end of input, answered here by `orElse` — so running out of input is handled where it happens
 * rather than crashing later.
 *
 * ```sh
 * ./mill examples.run jvm exe-jar examples/src/ -m Effects
 * echo "hello effects" | java -jar target/Effects.jar
 * ```
 */
def echo uses Console: Unit = printLine(readLine orElse "(no input)")

def main uses Console: Unit = echo
